<h1>Read-Only Plan for Splitting <code>App.tsx</code> (Milestone 2, Step 1)</h1>
<hr/>
<h2>1. Build Check</h2>
<h3>Build Status & Dependencies</h3>
<ul><li><b><code>node_modules</code> Status:</b> Missing. The directory <code>node_modules</code> does not exist in the project repository.</li></ul>
<ul><li><b><code>npm run build</code> Execution:</b> Not executed. Following the strict instruction (<i>"Do NOT run npm install without asking me first. If node_modules is missing, stop and ask. You MAY run npm run build if dependencies are already installed"</i>), <code>npm install</code> was <b>not</b> run. Because dependencies (<code>vite</code>, <code>react</code>, <code>@tailwindcss/vite</code>, etc.) are not yet installed locally, <code>npm run build</code> cannot run without first installing packages.</li></ul>
<ul><li><b>Stop & Question for You:</b> Would you like permission granted to run <code>npm install</code> (or <code>npm ci</code>) so dependencies can be installed and an initial production baseline build can be produced?</li></ul>
<h3>Lockfile Status</h3>
<ul><li><b><code>package-lock.json</code>:</b> <b>Not present and not committed.</b> There is no <code>package-lock.json</code> or <code>bun.lock</code>/<code>bun.lockb</code> anywhere in the repository or git history.</li></ul>
<h3>Output Folder & Git-Ignore</h3>
<ul><li>Default output folder configured by Vite is <code>dist/</code>.</li></ul>
<ul><li><code>.gitignore</code> (line 3) explicitly contains <code>dist/</code>, so all build artifacts will remain properly git-ignored.</li></ul>
<h3><code>vite.config.ts</code> Analysis for Plain Apache Hosting</h3>
<ul><li><b>Base Path:</b> <code>base</code> is not explicitly declared in <code>vite.config.ts</code>, which causes Vite to default to absolute root (<code>/</code>). If hosted inside an Apache subdirectory (e.g. <code>http://localhost/sarmelle/</code> or <code>/var/www/html/sarmelle/</code>), script and stylesheet assets linked as <code>/assets/...</code> will fail with 404 HTTP errors. When we configure the build for Apache, setting <code>base: './'</code> or <code>base: '/sarmelle/'</code> will be necessary.</li></ul>
<ul><li><b>Path Aliases:</b> Lines 10–12 configure <code>'@': path.resolve(__dirname, '.')</code> (repo root), <b>not</b> <code>./src</code>. Any relative import refactoring must respect this or adjust it intentionally.</li></ul>
<ul><li><b>AI Studio Settings:</b> Lines 14–20 specify dev-server HMR switches based on <code>process.env.DISABLE_HMR</code>. This is dev-server specific and does not block production static file builds.</li></ul>
<ul><li><b>Unused Dependencies in <code>package.json</code>:</b></li></ul>
<p>  * <code>@google/genai</code> (^2.4.0) is declared in <code>package.json</code>, but searching all files in <code>src/</code> confirms <b>it is never imported or used</b>.</p>
<p>  * <code>express</code>, <code>tsx</code>, and <code>dotenv</code> are declared in <code>package.json</code>, but are not referenced in the frontend bundle.</p>
<h3>Secrets and API Keys Audit</h3>
<ul><li><b>Client Code (<code>src/</code>):</b> <b>No API keys, access tokens, or hardcoded secrets exist</b> anywhere in <code>src/App.tsx</code>, <code>src/main.tsx</code>, or <code>index.html</code>. The payment modes are purely simulated UI mock states with placeholder test IDs (<code>pooja@okhdfcbank</code>, <code>4532 •••• •••• 8821</code>).</li></ul>
<ul><li><b><code>.env.example</code>:</b> Contains only non-sensitive local development placeholders (<code>rzp_test_placeholder</code>, <code>test_secret_placeholder</code>, <code>root</code>, <code>sarmelle_db</code>). No production credentials exist.</li></ul>
<hr/>
<h2>2. <code>App.tsx</code> Map</h2>
<p><code>src/App.tsx</code> has 5,770 lines containing the entire frontend application in a single file.</p>
