<h3>How Page Navigation Is Done Today</h3>
<ul><li><b>Mechanism:</b> Single Page Application (SPA) conditional rendering via React state (<code>currentView</code>).</li></ul>
<ul><li><b>Routing:</b> There is <b>no React Router, no URL pathname routing, and no window hash (<code>#</code>) routing</b>.</li></ul>
<ul><li><b>Persistence:</b> A single key <code>sarmelle_current_view</code> in <code>sessionStorage</code> restores the last opened screen on page refresh.</li></ul>
<hr/>
<h2>3. Proposed Split Plan</h2>
<p>To keep the application modular, maintainable, and prepared for future PHP/MySQL API integration without altering styling or behavior, we will organize the codebase cleanly into distinct folders:</p>
<h3>Proposed Folder Structure</h3>
<pre><code>src/
├── types/                     # TypeScript interfaces and shared types
│   ├── product.ts
│   ├── order.ts
│   └── campaign.ts
├── data/                      # Mock data (ready to be swapped for API endpoints)
│   ├── products.ts
│   ├── reviews.ts
│   ├── campaign.ts
│   ├── orders.ts
│   └── coupons.ts
├── context/                   # Shared global application states
│   ├── NavigationContext.tsx  # currentView, accountTab, modals
│   ├── CartContext.tsx        # cart, wishlist, coupon, price math
│   └── AuthContext.tsx        # userProfile, isLoggedIn, orders, returns
├── components/
│   ├── common/                # Reusable UI elements (Header, Footer, Announcements)
│   │   ├── Header.tsx
│   │   ├── MobileNav.tsx
│   │   └── Footer.tsx
│   ├── modals/                # Overlays and dialogs
│   │   ├── CartDrawer.tsx
│   │   ├── WishlistDrawer.tsx
│   │   ├── CheckoutModal.tsx
│   │   ├── AuthModal.tsx
│   │   ├── ReviewsModal.tsx
│   │   ├── SizeChartModal.tsx
│   │   ├── OrderTrackingModal.tsx
│   │   ├── ChangePasswordModal.tsx
│   │   └── ReturnModal.tsx
│   └── views/                 # Full screen page views
│       ├── HomeView.tsx
│       ├── CollectionView.tsx
│       ├── ProductDetailView.tsx
│       ├── AccountView.tsx
│       └── AdminView.tsx
├── App.tsx                    # Clean orchestrator rendering Header, active View, Modals, Footer
├── main.tsx
└── index.css</code></pre>
<hr/>
<h3>What Moves Where</h3>
<h4>1. <code>src/types/</code></h4>
<ul><li><code>product.ts</code>: <code>Product</code>, <code>ProductReview</code>.</li></ul>
<ul><li><code>campaign.ts</code>: <code>HeroSlide</code>, <code>PromoBanner</code>, <code>FeaturedBlock</code>, <code>LookbookConfig</code>.</li></ul>
<ul><li><code>order.ts</code>: <code>UserOrderItem</code>, <code>UserOrder</code>, <code>UserReturn</code>.</li></ul>
<h4>2. <code>src/data/</code></h4>
<ul><li><code>products.ts</code>: <code>SAMPLE_PRODUCTS</code>.</li></ul>
<ul><li><code>reviews.ts</code>: <code>SAMPLE_REVIEWS</code>.</li></ul>
<ul><li><code>campaign.ts</code>: <code>SAMPLE_HERO_SLIDES</code>, <code>SAMPLE_PROMO_BANNERS</code>, <code>SAMPLE_FEATURED_BLOCKS</code>, <code>DEFAULT_LOOKBOOK</code>.</li></ul>
<ul><li><code>orders.ts</code>: <code>SAMPLE_USER_ORDERS</code>, <code>SAMPLE_USER_RETURNS</code>.</li></ul>
<ul><li><code>coupons.ts</code>: Available promo coupon definitions (<code>DIWALI30</code>, <code>WELCOME10</code>, <code>FESTIVE500</code>).</li></ul>
<h4>3. State Strategy: Context vs Local</h4>
<ul><li><b>Shared in Context:</b></li></ul>
<p>  * <code>CartContext</code>: <code>cart</code>, <code>cartOpen</code>, <code>wishlist</code>, <code>wishlistOpen</code>, <code>coupon</code>, cart calculations (<code>subtotal</code>, <code>discount</code>, <code>shipping</code>, <code>total</code>), cart mutation handlers (<code>addToCart</code>, <code>updateCartQuantity</code>, <code>removeCartItem</code>, <code>toggleWishlist</code>).</p>
<p>  * <code>AuthContext</code>: <code>isLoggedIn</code>, <code>userProfile</code>, <code>userOrders</code>, <code>userReturns</code>, active order tracking, return modal state.</p>
<p>  * <code>NavigationContext</code>: <code>currentView</code>, <code>setCurrentView</code>, <code>selectedProduct</code> (active PDP item), navigation filters.</p>
<ul><li><b>Kept Local to Components:</b></li></ul>
<p>  * Homepage: <code>currentHeroSlide</code>, <code>isHeroHovered</code>, carousel swipe refs, <code>activeProductTab</code>.</p>
<p>  * Collection: Catalog filter inputs (<code>selectedFabric</code>, <code>selectedColorFilter</code>, <code>maxPrice</code>, <code>sortBy</code>, <code>visibleProductsCount</code>).</p>
<p>  * Product Detail: <code>selectedProductColor</code>, <code>selectedProductSize</code>, <code>activeProductImageIdx</code>, accordion open/close.</p>
<p>  * Checkout Modal: <code>checkoutStep</code>, <code>deliveryAddress</code>, <code>paymentMethod</code>, form validation states.</p>
<p>  * Admin View: Admin tabs and local CMS form buffers.</p>
<hr/>
<h3>Safe Order of Extraction (Incremental Small Steps)</h3>
<p>Each step is self-contained and allows running <code>npm run build</code> immediately to guarantee zero syntax or typing regressions before moving to the next.</p>
<ol><li><b>Step 1 — Types Extraction:</b> Create <code>src/types/</code> and extract all interfaces from lines 16–429 & 627–668. Import them back into <code>App.tsx</code>.</li></ol>
<ol><li><b>Step 2 — Mock Data Extraction:</b> Create <code>src/data/</code> and extract static sample arrays/objects from lines 36–780. Import them into <code>App.tsx</code>.</li></ol>
<ol><li><b>Step 3 — Global Modals Extraction:</b> Extract standalone modals that have minimal coupling into <code>src/components/modals/</code>:</li></ol>
<p>   * <code>SizeChartModal.tsx</code></p>
<p>   * <code>ReviewsModal.tsx</code></p>
<p>   * <code>ChangePasswordModal.tsx</code></p>
<ol><li><b>Step 4 — Context Setup:</b> Introduce <code>CartContext.tsx</code> and <code>AuthContext.tsx</code> to cleanly wrap the app, eliminating prop-drilling.</li></ol>
<ol><li><b>Step 5 — Heavy Modals & Drawers Extraction:</b></li></ol>
<p>   * <code>CartDrawer.tsx</code></p>
<p>   * <code>WishlistDrawer.tsx</code></p>
<p>   * <code>AuthModal.tsx</code></p>
<p>   * <code>OrderTrackingModal.tsx</code></p>
<p>   * <code>ReturnModal.tsx</code></p>
<p>   * <code>CheckoutModal.tsx</code></p>
<ol><li><b>Step 6 — Layout Components:</b> Extract <code>Header.tsx</code>, <code>MobileNav.tsx</code>, and <code>Footer.tsx</code> into <code>src/components/common/</code>.</li></ol>
<ol><li><b>Step 7 — Page Views Extraction:</b></li></ol>
<p>   * <code>HomeView.tsx</code> (L1552–L2103)</p>
<p>   * <code>CollectionView.tsx</code> (L2104–L2628)</p>
<p>   * <code>ProductDetailView.tsx</code> (L2629–L2987)</p>
<p>   * <code>AccountView.tsx</code> (L2988–L3516)</p>
<p>   * <code>AdminView.tsx</code> (L3517–L4010)</p>
<ol><li><b>Step 8 — Final App Assembly:</b> Reduce <code>App.tsx</code> down to a clean ~60-line top-level provider & view router.</li></ol>
<hr/>
