<hr/>
<h2>5. Risks and Unknowns</h2>
<ol><li><b>Missing Lockfile (<code>package-lock.json</code>):</b></li></ol>
<p>   <i> </i>Risk:* Running <code>npm install</code> without a lockfile could install newer patch/minor releases of packages (e.g. Tailwind v4 or React 19 sub-dependencies) that could introduce unintended deprecations.</p>
<p>   <i> </i>Mitigation:* We should run <code>npm install</code>, verify package versions, and commit the generated <code>package-lock.json</code> once approved.</p>
<ol><li><b>Vite Base Path for Apache Hosting:</b></li></ol>
<p>   <i> </i>Risk:* The default <code>base: '/'</code> in <code>vite.config.ts</code> will break asset loading if hosted under a subdirectory in Apache.</p>
<p>   <i> </i>Mitigation:* Add <code>base: './'</code> to <code>vite.config.ts</code> during the build configuration step.</p>
<ol><li><b>SessionStorage Desynchronization:</b></li></ol>
<p>   <i> </i>Risk:* If navigation state is split across multiple contexts without keeping the <code>sessionStorage</code> synchronization listeners, browser page reloads could revert to the homepage unexpectedly.</p>
<p>   <i> </i>Mitigation:* Centralize <code>sessionStorage</code> persistence in <code>NavigationContext</code>.</p>
<ol><li><b>Tailwind v4 CSS Scanning:</b></li></ol>
<p>   <i> </i>Risk:<i> Tailwind v4 uses dynamic file scanning. Moving JSX components to newly created subfolders (<code>src/components/</code>, <code>src/pages/</code>) must ensure that Tailwind still scans all files inside <code>src/</i><i>/</i>.{ts,tsx}</code>.</p>
<p>   <i> </i>Mitigation:* Verify styles remain active after extracting the first component.</p>
</body></html>